GitLab sast-rules, selected for Pitangus
========================================

Source: https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/security-products/sast-rules
Version: v2.10.1 (commit 53bf5cf6df3c51b6c02110f5a638b5e6213666cd, 2026-09-21)

259 rule files, unchanged, each with its upstream license header. SHA256SUMS pins them.

Licenses of what is included:
- MIT (c) GitLab Inc. (238 files): LICENSE.
- Apache License 2.0 (c) gosec authors (21 Go files derived from https://github.com/securego/gosec): LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.
- 6 JavaScript files declare an origin in eslint-plugin-security (Apache License 2.0,
  https://github.com/eslint-community/eslint-plugin-security): LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

Left out, with the reason (provenance checked file by file against each header, the upstream README and, for
every MIT or Apache candidate, the semgrep-rules repository of the same language):

